is a scientist, I can\'t be in the committee.But in this case, I isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\nSo, this seems possible.\n\nWait, but then Y could be chairman.But Y isn\'t an option for chairman in Year 2 because the options are A) F, B) G, C) Y, D) I.\n\nWait, but in this case, Y is a scientist, so he can\'t be chairman because the chairman must be a member of Year 1\'s committee, which includes H, F, V, Z.So, Y isn\'t in Year 1\'s committee, so he can\'t be chairman in Year 2.\n\nWait, no, the chairman must be a member of Year 1\'s committee, which is H, F, V, Z.So, Y isn\'t in Year 1\'s committee, so he can\'t be chairman in Year 2.\n\nTherefore, Y can\'t be chairman in Year 2.\n\nSo, the only possible options are F and Z.\n\nBut Z isn\'t an option, so the answer must be F.\n\nWait, but earlier when considering Z as chairman, we had two possibilities: Z, G, I, Y or Z, F, G, Y.\n\nBut in both cases, Z is chairman, but Z isn\'t an option.So, the only possible chairman from the options is F.\n\nWait, but let me check again.\n\nWait, in Year 2, if the chairman is F, then the committee is F, G, Y, Z.\n\nBut let\'s check if that\'s allowed.\n\n- G and V: G is a judge, V isn\'t in the committee, so that\'s fine.\n\n- H and Y: H is out, Y is in, so that\'s fine.\n\n- Only one of I or V: I isn\'t in, V isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\nSo, that\'s valid.\n\nIf the chairman is Z, then the committee is Z, G, I, Y or Z, F, G, Y.\n\nBut in both cases, Z is chairman, but Z isn\'t an option.So, the only possible chairman from the options is F.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any other possibility.\n\nWait, could the chairman be G?\n\nIf G is chairman, then G is a judge.So, the other judge must be F or I.\n\nIf the other judge is F, then the scientists must be two from V, Y, Z, but V can\'t be with G, so scientists would be Y and Z.\n\nBut then, the I/V constraint: since G is a judge, V can\'t be a scientist.So, scientists would be Y and Z, which is fine.\n\nSo, Year 2 committee: G, F, Y, Z.\n\nWait, but let\'s check the constraints.\n\n- G and V: G is a judge, V isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\n- H and Y: H is out, Y is in, so that\'s fine.\n\n- Only one of I or V: I isn\'t in, V isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\nSo, this seems possible.\n\nWait, but G is a judge, so the other judge is F.\n\nSo, Year 2 committee: G, F, Y, Z.\n\nBut wait, in Year 1, the judges were H and F. So, F is still in the committee, which is allowed because F was a member in Year 1.\n\nBut wait, the chairman of Year 2 is G, who is a judge.So, G is a judge, and F is also a judge.So, that\'s fine.\n\nBut let\'s check if this violates any constraints.\n\n- G and V: G is a judge, V isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\n- H and Y: H is out, Y is in, so that\'s fine.\n\n- Only one of I or V: I isn\'t in, V isn\'t in, so that\'s fine.\n\nSo, this seems possible.\n\nWait, but then G could be chairman.But G isn\'t an option.The options are A) F, B) G, C) Y, D) I.\n\nSo, if G is possible, then B) G is an option.\n\nWait, but earlier when I considered G as chairman, I thought it was possible, but I might have made a mistake.\n\nWait, let me re-examine.\n\nIf G is chairman, then the committee is G, F, Y, Z.\n\nBut wait, in Year 1, the judges were H and F. So, F is still in the committee, which is allowed because F was a member in Year 1.\n\nBut the chairman of Year 2 is G, who wasn\'t a chairman in Year 1, but he is a judge, so he can be a member.\n\nWait, but the constraint is that the chairman of Year 2 must be a member of Year 1\'s committee.G wasn\'t a chairman in Year 1, but he is a judge in Year 1.So, he is a member of Year 1\'s committee, so he can be chairman in Year 2.\n\nSo, that\'s allowed.\n\nTherefore, G could be chairman in Year 2.\n\nWait, but earlier when I considered G as chairman, I thought it was possible, but I might have missed something.\n\nWait, let me check again.\n\nYear 2 committee: G, F, Y, Z.\n\n- G is chairman, judge.\n\n- F is judge.\n\n- Y and Z are scientists.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- G and V: G is a judge, V isn\'t in, so okay.\n\n- H and Y: H is out, Y is in, okay.\n\n- Only one of I or V: I isn\'t in, V isn\'t in, okay.\n\nSo, this seems valid.\n\nTherefore, G could be chairman in Year 2.\n\nBut wait, in Year 1, the judges were H and F. So, F is still in the committee, which is allowed because F was a member in Year 1.\n\nSo, G can be chairman in Year 2.\n\nWait, but earlier when I considered G as chairman, I thought it was possible, but I might have missed that F is still in the committee.\nDespite the initial considerations, G cannot be chairman in Year 2 due to not being a member of Year 1\'s committee, contrary to earlier beliefs. This means the only viable chairman from the options is F, making the answer A) F.</think>.\n\nThe correct answer is A) F.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1. **Year 1 Committee Composition:**.\n   - H is chairman (chairman must retire in Year 2).\n   - Judges: H and F (since G and I can\'t be with G due to the G-V constraint, and V can\'t be with H).\n   - Scientists: V and Z (since V can\'t be with G, and Y can\'t be with H).\n\n2. **Year 2 Constraints:**.\n   - Chairman must be a member of Year 1\'s committee (H, F, V, Z).\n   - H retires, so he can\'t be chairman in Year 2.\n   - Possible Year 2 chairmen: F, V, Z.\n\n3. **Evaluating Possible Chairmen for Year 2:**.\n   - **V as Chairman:** Leads to conflicts with G\'s constraint and I/V constraint. Impossible.\n   - **Z as Chairman:** Possible but Z isn\'t an option.\n   - **F as Chairman:** .\n     - Judges: F and G (G can\'t be with V, so V isn\'t in the committee).\n     - Scientists: Y and Z (V isn\'t in the committee, satisfying I/V constraint).\n     - All constraints are satisfied.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Only F can be the chairman in Year 2 based on the given options. Therefore, my final option is: ']]  5%|5         | 30/600 [02:28<1:36:07, 10.12s/it]
