on quality, human resource accounting is more necessary. This directly corresponds to the description of the country in question.\n     - Therefore, this option can be inferred.\n   \n   - **Option D:** \"The competition of human resources has become the key factor of social development.\"\n     - The text mentions that human resource development, utilization, and management are key factors in societal and economic growth. However, it does not explicitly state that human resource competition has become the key factor of social development.\n     - Thus, this option cannot be inferred.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Based on the analysis, the only option that can be directly inferred from the text is **Option C**.\n</think>\n\n**Answer: C) The population of our country is large and the quality of the population is relatively poor.**",
