messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.", "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the given options is not an example of the invisible curriculum.Let me start by understanding what invisible curriculum means.From the context provided, invisible curriculum refers to informal and unconscious learning that isn't clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.So, it's about the things that happen outside of formal lessons that students pick up on, like through activities, relationships, or experiences.\n\nNow, looking at the question, it's asking which option is NOT an invisible curriculum.That means I need to find the one that's part of the formal curriculum or is clearly specified.\n\nLet's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.Hmm, military training is usually part of the formal curriculum, right?It's a structured activity that's planned and part of the school's program.So this might be considered part of the visible curriculum, not invisible.\n\nOption B: When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.Wait, teaching courses are part of the formal curriculum.But the part about cultivating interest in learning and teaching—does that come from the course itself or from something else?I'm a bit confused here.The teaching courses are formal, but maybe the interest part is something the students pick up on outside, like through interactions or experiences.I'm not sure yet.\n\nOption C: A university sets up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.This sounds like a planned event.The school motto and study style are part of the formal curriculum because they're specified and taught.So this is probably visible curriculum.\n\nOption D: Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.Extracurricular activities are usually outside the regular school program.They're informal and not part of the planned curriculum, so this would be invisible curriculum.\n\nWait, so the question is asking which is NOT an invisible curriculum.So, the correct answer would be the one that's part of the formal curriculum.\n\nLooking back, Option A is about military training, which is part of the formal curriculum.So it's not invisible.Option B is about teaching courses, which are formal, but the interest part might be part of the formal curriculum as well.Option C is clearly formal.Option D is extracurricular, so it's invisible.\n\nSo the question is which is NOT invisible.So the answer should be the one that's part of the formal curriculum.That would be either A, B, or C.\n\nWait, let me think again.The question is asking which is NOT an invisible curriculum.So the correct answer is the one that is part of the formal curriculum.\n\nOption A: Military training is part of the formal curriculum, so it's not invisible.So A is not an invisible curriculum.\n\nOption B: Teaching courses are part of the formal curriculum, so the interest in learning might be part of the formal curriculum as well.A is invisible because it's not part of the formal curriculum.</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: "]] 38%|###7      | 227/600 [08:44<01:08,  5.42it/s]
