messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country's famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen's one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun's fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman's eyebrows are cold and stubborn", '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main expression of the given text.Let me start by reading the context carefully.The text talks about public speeches in China, mentioning that some speakers are verbose while others are concise.It then gives an example of Mr. Zou Taofen, who delivered a very short speech of 33 words.The speech is praised for being memorable and profound, even though it\'s just one sentence.\n\nThe question asks which option correctly captures the main idea of the text.The options are A, B, C, D. Let me go through each one.\n\nOption A says that short speeches, like Zou Taofen\'s, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects.That seems to align with the context because the text highlights how a short sentence can be impactful.\n\nOption B mentions the phrase "unyielding in battle" outlining Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit.The text does talk about Lu Xun\'s sacrifice, but it doesn\'t explicitly use that phrase.It\'s more about the brevity of the speech rather than the fighting spirit.\n\nThe text primarily emphasizes the fame and admiration of Lu Xun, not the effectiveness of his speech. It doesn\'t discuss the power of short, impactful speeches, as shown by Zou\'s example. The correct answer should be D.</think>.\n\nThe main expression of the text is that short speeches, like Zou Taofen\'s, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
