messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nNo matter how rich and wonderful the original works are, the adaptation of literary classics into TV dramas is a re-creation. TV dramas should not only present the complex and heavy themes of the original as much as possible, but also integrate the stories into the fate of characters through adaptation. The historical changes of the ancient land, the life reflection of national survival, the glory and decline of Confucian culture, the suppression and publicity of human desire. The motif of literary classics must be reinterpreted through adaptation. Moreover, no matter how to change, the advance of the plot, the shaping of the characters and the development of the plot should conform to the inherent behavior logic of the characters.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, regarding the principle of adapting literary classics into TV series, which of the following articles is not covered?\n# Options:\nA) To highlight the themes of literary classics\nB) There must be a clearer thread\nC) Should have reasonable internal logic\nD) Use necessary exaggeration', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out this question about adapting literary classics into TV series.The context given talks about how TV dramas are a re-creation of the original works.It mentions that TV dramas should present the complex and heavy themes as much as possible, integrate the stories into character fates, and that the historical changes, life reflections, cultural glories and declines, and suppression of human desires are all part of the adaptation.It also says that the motif must be reinterpreted, and the plot, character shaping, and plot development should follow the inherent behavior logic of the characters.\n\nThe question is asking which article is not covered based on this information.The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me break d