conclusion is already that extrinsics aren't relevant.So adding D would make it more explicit.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the correct answer is B because it's necessary to have that premise to reach the conclusion.But I'm not sure.\n\nWait, the question is about which option, when added, makes the conclusion follow.So if the premises already include that we should focus on intrinsic, then the conclusion is already there.So adding B doesn't change anything.But the question is about adding an option to the premises to make the conclusion follow.\n\nWait, perhaps the correct answer is B because it's necessary to have that premise to reach the conclusion.But I'm not entirely sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the correct answer is D because it directly supports the conclusion by stating that symbolizing is extrinsic, thus irrelevant.\n\nI'm a bit confused now.Let me try to think differently.\n\nThe conclusion is that aesthetic relevance is intrinsic, so extrinsics are irrelevant.The premises already state that.So adding any premise that supports this would make the conclusion more solid.\n\nOption B is just restating the premise, so it doesn't add anything new.Option D says symbolizing is extrinsic, which aligns with the conclusion that extrinsics are irrelevant.So adding D would make the conclusion more explicit.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.\n\nWait, but the question is about which option, when added, makes the conclusion follow.So if the premises already include that we should focus on intrinsic, then the conclusion is already there.So adding D would make it more explicit, but the conclusion would still follow.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the correct answer is B because it's necessary to have that premise to reach the conclusion.But I'm not sure.I don't need to analyze the structure further. Both intrinsic and extrinsic properties are important. Aesthetic relevance is not solely intrinsic. Therefore, adding a premise would change the conclusion. The question is not abou