isters.  \n  - There are three boys (A, B, D) and two girls (C, E). So, there are more boys than girls. This is incorrect.\n  \n- **Option D:** A ranks third among the six brothers and sisters.  \n  - The siblings are A, B, C, D, E. A is the oldest, D is the second oldest, and B is the youngest. So, A ranks first, D ranks second, and B ranks third. This is correct.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\boxed{D}",
